    "faq": {
      "type": "neu-faq",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "FAQ",
        "heading": "Ask us anything?",
        "faq_schema": true,
        "padding_top": 80,
        "padding_bottom": 80
      },
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "When will I notice a difference?",
            "answer": "<p>In clinical studies, daily NR raised blood NAD+ levels within 2 weeks, and they stayed raised with continued use (Conze et al., 2019). How that feels differs from person to person, so we suggest taking one shot every day for at least 8 weeks before you judge it.</p>",
            "open": true
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does the subscription work?",
            "answer": "<p>Your first order ships immediately. 24-shot subscriptions renew every 3 weeks and 36-shot subscriptions every 4 weeks. You can skip, pause or cancel any time from your account — no fees, no questions.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is Nicotinamide Riboside (NR)?",
            "answer": "<p>NR is a form of vitamin B3 and a direct precursor to NAD+, the molecule every cell needs to produce energy. NAD+ levels fall by around half between the ages of 40 and 60, and NR is one of the most studied ways to raise them.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is NEU+ vegan and gluten-free?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. NEU+ is vegan, gluten-free, sugar-free and made in the UK. Each batch is third-party tested and Informed Sport certified for safe use by athletes.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Delivery and returns",
            "answer": "<p>Free UK delivery for subscribers. Orders typically dispatched within 1–2 business days. 30-day money-back guarantee on first orders.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "nmn": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "NR or NMN: what's the difference?",
            "answer": "<p>Both are NAD+ precursors. NR has the larger body of completed human clinical trials, showing it is absorbed (Trammell et al., 2016) and, in a randomised, placebo-controlled trial, that it raises blood NAD+ (Martens et al., 2018). NMN is a larger molecule with far fewer human trials so far. That's why NEU+ uses NR.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "format": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why a shot rather than capsules or an IV drip?",
            "answer": "<p>One 60ml shot gives you 300mg NR with TMG and vitamin C, so there are no pills to swallow and it fits into your morning. NR taken by mouth is absorbed and raises NAD+ levels (Trammell et al., 2016). IV NAD+ drips need a clinic visit; NEU+ is made for steady daily use, which is how NR has been studied.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "safety": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is NR safe to take long term?",
            "answer": "<p>NR has been well tolerated in human trials. In a randomised, placebo-controlled study, healthy adults took up to 1,000mg daily for 8 weeks with no serious side effects (Conze et al., 2019). Each NEU+ shot contains 300mg, and unlike niacin, NR doesn't cause flushing. If you're pregnant, breastfeeding, under 18, taking medication or have a medical condition, check with a healthcare professional first.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "harrods": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Where can I buy NEU+?",
            "answer": "<p>Here on neu-plus.com, and in store at <a href=\"https://www.harrods.com/en-gb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Harrods, London</a>, our exclusive retail partner.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        }
